## Why This Is Asked

Tests dynamic graph data structures with parallel edges and per-node statistics, a realistic scenario in routing or network monitoring.

## Key Concepts

- per-node multiset keyed by (weight, edge_id)
- order-statistic tree for kth largest
- two-endpoint synchronization on add/erase/update
- sum maintenance for O(1) incident sum reads

## Code Example

```javascript
class Node {
  constructor() { this.edges = new Treap(); this.sum = 0; }
  add(weight, id) { this.edges.insert(weight, id); this.sum += weight; }
  remove(weight, id) { this.edges.erase(weight, id); this.sum -= weight; }
  kthLargest(k) { return this.edges.kthLargest(k); }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to handle memory pressure with millions of edges?
- How would you extend to directed graphs with asymmetric weights?
